From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:05:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Mirror bounding box coordinates for entity section scans

Entity box queries (pushing, target goals, sensors, collisions) test
every entity in the scanned sections, loading the entity and then its
separately allocated AABB, which is replaced on every move and so
scattered on the heap. Entities now also keep the six box coordinates
in plain fields, written together with bb in setBoundingBox, its only
writer. The section scans read them on tick threads, where entities
move; other threads still read the AABB, since the six fields are not
updated atomically. JMH, 1,100-entity section: 3.52 to 2.56 ms per
query round; no difference when the section fits in cache.

diff --git a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/ChunkEntitySlices.java b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/ChunkEntitySlices.java
